            <div xml:id="d93">

                <pb facs="0097" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg85"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860D.00/935: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Greene</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-30T12:00:00+01:00">October 30,
                            1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:01 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>700. The Finnish Minister who has just returned from 8 days in Finland during
                    which he was in intimate contact with President Ryti, <pb facs="0098" n="86"
                        xml:id="pg86"/> Prime Minister, Foreign Minister and Minister of Defense
                    told me following:</p>
                <p>Above group in constant collaboration really governs Finland. Tanner because of
                    his position as head of largest political group and as Cabinet member is also in
                    close contact but is usually more independent in his views such as those
                    expressed on September 14 (Department’s 201, October 4, 4 p.m., to Helsinki)
                    which Tanner has subsequently been told were not in accordance with basic policy
                    of others. Tanner’s radio speech October 28 for example was more in line.</p>
                <p>Minister said that Finland still maintained that it would continue fighting only
                    until such objectives as were needed for its strategic and political safety were
                    reached and that decision of extent of this territory would and could be
                    determined only by Finland; that Government still had no intention of continuing
                    war for any other purpose. He said that Government plans reasonably soon to
                    explain to Parliament its post-war territorial objectives but that until then
                    these plans will be kept secret, not even Swedish Government being informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Greene</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
